# Claude Code Commands

A comprehensive list of available slash commands in the Claude Code CLI.

## General Commands
- `/help`: Displays the help menu with available commands and usage information.
- `/clear`: Clears the current conversation history from the terminal.
- `/config`: Opens the configuration menu to adjust settings, model preferences, and behavior.
- `/reset`: Resets the current session.

## Memory & Project Context
- `/remember`: Manages persistent project memory. Use this to save facts, preferences, or project goals.
- `/init`: Initializes a `CLAUDE.md` file with codebase documentation to provide better context for the agent.

## Artifacts & Design
- `/artifacts`: Lists the artifacts you own or that have been shared with you.
- `/design-login`: Authenticates you with the Claude design system.
- `/design-sync`: Synchronizes a local component library with a design-system project.

## Task & Workflow Management
- `/tasks`: Lists and manages active background tasks, agents, and monitors.
- `/workflows`: Monitors the live progress of active multi-agent workflows.
- `/loop`: Runs a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g., `/loop 5m /foo`).

## Other Commands
- `/compact`: Compacts the conversation history to save tokens.
- `/skill-doctor`: Runs a diagnostic on available skills and their configurations.
